<title>TAIWAN: First Int'l August sales up 9.0 pct.</title>
<headline>First Int'l August sales up 9.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>First International Computer Inc, Taiwan's second largest computer firm, said on Monday its sales in August rose 9.0 percent to T$2.555 billion from August 1995.</p>
<p>Its combined sales for the first eight months were up 21 percent to T$18.169 billion from the corresponding period in 1995, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company did not give profit figures.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
